1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,383
The data of a report rarely has the number you need:

2
00:00:04,383 --> 00:00:08,583
minutes instead of seconds, a Long or Short label, an answer rate.

3
00:00:08,583 --> 00:00:12,840
A calculated field works it out with a formula, like a spreadsheet.

4
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:16,340
This video builds five of them, in the Report Builder.

5
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:23,507
A report shows what is stored:

6
00:00:23,507 --> 00:00:26,289
seconds of waiting, dates, names.

7
00:00:26,289 --> 00:00:30,710
People ask for minutes, labels, ages in days, and rates.

8
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:34,949
A calculated field is a formula with a name.

9
00:00:34,949 --> 00:00:41,160
Once it exists, you drag it onto columns, filters and visuals like any other field.

10
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:44,492
A formula never stops the report:

11
00:00:44,492 --> 00:00:48,730
dividing by zero or a missing value gives an empty result.

12
00:00:52,933 --> 00:00:54,857
This report lists calls.

13
00:00:54,857 --> 00:00:58,643
In the Data pane, under Calculated fields, click New.

14
00:00:59,095 --> 00:01:04,173
Enter a Label, such as Wait in minutes, and a Name that formulas will use:

15
00:01:04,173 --> 00:01:07,919
a letter first, then letters, digits and underscores.

16
00:01:07,919 --> 00:01:10,395
The name cannot be changed later.

17
00:01:10,884 --> 00:01:12,383
Write the Formula.

18
00:01:12,383 --> 00:01:17,751
Click a field in the Fields list, and it is written for you, in square brackets.

19
00:01:17,751 --> 00:01:19,624
Then divide it by sixty.

20
00:01:20,076 --> 00:01:21,175
Click Check.

21
00:01:21,175 --> 00:01:25,146
The builder shows the type of the result, or what is wrong.

22
00:01:25,146 --> 00:01:26,246
Click Apply.

23
00:01:26,696 --> 00:01:30,051
The new field is listed under Calculated fields.

24
00:01:30,051 --> 00:01:34,276
Drag it onto Columns, and the preview shows it for every call.

25
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:40,543
A formula can give a label.

26
00:01:40,543 --> 00:01:46,233
This one answers Long when the talk time is ten minutes or more, and Short otherwise.

27
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:47,859
Text goes in quotes.

28
00:01:53,926 --> 00:01:55,905
A formula can fill a gap.

29
00:01:55,905 --> 00:02:01,266
COALESCE gives the queue name, or Outbound campaigns when a call has no queue.

30
00:02:10,975 --> 00:02:13,403
And a formula can work with dates.

31
00:02:13,403 --> 00:02:16,681
DATEDIFF counts the days from the call to today.

32
00:02:16,681 --> 00:02:22,085
The Functions list explains every function, and a click writes it into the formula.

33
00:02:26,288 --> 00:02:30,734
A formula that uses an aggregate function, such as SUM or COUNT, is

34
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:32,987
worked out once for each group.

35
00:02:32,987 --> 00:02:35,788
This report counts calls for each queue.

36
00:02:37,018 --> 00:02:40,912
The answer rate adds one for each call that has an answer time,

37
00:02:40,912 --> 00:02:43,226
and divides by the number of calls.

38
00:02:43,226 --> 00:02:47,853
Inside such a formula, every field must be inside an aggregate function, and

39
00:02:47,853 --> 00:02:49,998
Check tells you when one is not.

40
00:02:50,452 --> 00:02:54,747
Apply it, drag it onto Columns, and give it the format P zero,

41
00:02:54,747 --> 00:02:56,894
so it shows as a percentage.

42
00:02:56,894 --> 00:02:59,042
Each queue now has its rate.

43
00:03:03,242 --> 00:03:04,995
Minutes, not seconds:

44
00:03:04,995 --> 00:03:09,672
divide the seconds, and give the column a format with one decimal.

45
00:03:10,422 --> 00:03:12,226
A label to group by:

46
00:03:12,226 --> 00:03:18,682
Large and Small orders, Long and Short calls, or Business and Personal email addresses.

47
00:03:19,432 --> 00:03:21,448
A rate once per group:

48
00:03:21,448 --> 00:03:26,632
answered over offered, converted over created, refunded over sold.

49
00:03:28,632 --> 00:03:31,584
A calculated field is a formula with a name.

50
00:03:31,584 --> 00:03:35,127
Check it, apply it, and drag it wherever a field goes.

51
00:03:35,127 --> 00:03:38,906
Other features of the site can add functions of their own.

52
00:03:38,906 --> 00:03:40,442
Thanks for watching.

